==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{der|en|la|centriolum}}, diminutive of {{m|la|centrum}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛntɹɪˌəʊl/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|biology}} A barrel-shaped [[microtubule]] structure found in most animal [[cell]]s, important in the process of [[mitosis]] (nuclear division).
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Journal of Morphology|volume=11|issue=1|year=1895|title=Archoplasm, centrosome, and chromatin in the sea-urchin egg|author=Edmund B. Wilson|passage=The aster is at this period closely similar to those of ''Ascaris'' at certain periods, as figured by Boveri, and the red mass with its central group of granules corresponds exactly, I think, to Boveri's "centrosome" with its "Centralkorn" or "'''centriole'''" ("centrosphere" with its "centrosome" in Strasburger's terminology).}}

